# LiveKit Documentation Is the Source of Truth

Before implementing or modifying any LiveKit-related feature, check the latest LiveKit documentation through the configured LiveKit MCP server.

Applies to: Agents SDK, sessions, OpenAI Realtime, STT/LLM/TTS, VAD, turn detection, interruptions, SIP/telephony, Twilio, dispatch, rooms, function tools, lifecycle, deployment, workers, metrics, auth tokens.

Never rely only on memory or outdated examples.

Before writing LiveKit code:

1. Search relevant LiveKit docs through MCP.
2. Confirm current APIs, imports, class names, config fields, and recommended patterns.
3. Use the latest non-deprecated approach.
4. Follow official LiveKit examples where applicable.
5. Do not invent LiveKit methods, properties, events, or config options.
6. If docs and existing code conflict, explain the conflict and update to the documented production approach.

Add a brief code comment only when a non-obvious decision comes directly from LiveKit behavior.
